dialect protocol
protocol stdio.obj.mutations
version 1
schema stdio.obj.op
start op

# P2-FG1: `protocol::OpBinary::encode_op`/`decode_op` (../🦀️.rs `OpCodecs` region)
# forward straight to `dsl::variants_binary::encode_op`/`decode_op`
# (`🗣️dsl/🦀️.rs`'s `OpRt` region) — this was ALREADY real binary before this wave
# touched it, NOT the F6-era `print_op().into_bytes()` text-as-binary shortcut (confirmed by
# direct reading, not assumed: `encode_op` calls `os_pack::encode_record_body`, never
# `print_op`) — same already-real situation `stdio.txt`'s own mutations protocol file documents.
# Layout, byte-for-byte, per that helper's own doc comment (`OP_BINARY_FORMAT`): a fixed
# `format` byte (always `1`), the matched `ObjMutation` variant's ordinal as a `varint`
# (declaration order, `NoMutation` dropped: `SetSnapshot`=0, `InsertVertex`=1, `RemoveVertex`=2,
# `SetVertex`=3, `InsertTexcoord`=4, `RemoveTexcoord`=5, `SetTexcoord`=6, `InsertNormal`=7,
# `RemoveNormal`=8, `SetNormal`=9, `InsertFace`=10, `RemoveFace`=11, `SetFace`=12,
# `SetGroup`=13, `RemoveGroup`=14, `SetObject`=15, `RemoveObject`=16, `SetMtllib`=17,
# `SetUsemtl`=18, `SetSmoothingGroups`=19, `SetUnknownStatements`=20 — `dsl::DslVariants::
# variants()`'s own emission order, matching `../🦀️.rs`'s `ObjMutation` declaration),
# then the variant's own field payload, `os_pack::encode_record_body(spec, record)` — itself a
# varint-prefixed STRING-SYMBOL TABLE followed by a generic, self-describing per-field-id
# TAG+value wire (`🎒️pack/🔢️value/🦀️.rs`'s `encode_record_body`/`encode_record_fields`).
# This inner wire is the FRAMEWORK's own generic record-body encoding — shared verbatim by every
# `#[derive(dsl::DslRecord)]`/`DslOps`/`DslDiff` type in the whole repo, not anything specific to
# `stdio.obj` — and is genuinely NOT expressible by this dialect's `Array`/`Ref`/`repeat`
# primitives as they stand today (no dynamic per-field TAG dispatch keyed by a runtime field-id,
# no symbol-table back-reference resolution) — the SAME `txt-opbinary-record-body-wire-is-
# framework-generic` mechanism gap `stdio.txt`'s own pilot wave first named. Modeled honestly:
# `format`/`ordinal` are genuinely, individually byte-walked and validated; the remaining
# record-body bytes are one opaque tail.
framing record
field format u8
field ordinal varint
chain bytes
